# Copy to .env for local development. .env is gitignored; this file is not.
# On Render these are set in the dashboard, not here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECRET_KEY=change-me
MAILJET_API_KEY=
MAILJET_SECRET_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: SMS lead alerts
#
# A contractor wins the job by calling back first, so leads should hit a phone,
# not just an inbox. Set ONE of the two blocks below. With neither set, nothing
# is texted and the lead email behaves exactly as it always has.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Option A - Twilio. Costs about $1.15/month for the number plus $0.008 a
# message (so a few dollars a year at this volume), and it actually arrives.
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
# TWILIO_FROM=+16195550123        # the Twilio number, E.164 format
# ALERT_SMS_TO=+16198071227       # the phone that should ring, E.164 format

# Option B - carrier email-to-SMS gateway. Free and reuses Mailjet, but you
# have to know the carrier and they increasingly filter mail from bulk senders,
# so treat it as a stopgap rather than the long-term answer.
#   Verizon   <number>@vtext.com
#   AT&T      <number>@txt.att.net
#   T-Mobile  <number>@tmomail.net
# ALERT_SMS_EMAIL=6198071227@vtext.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set automatically by Render; only needed locally if 5000 is taken.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PORT=5000
